When generating or modifying code for the First1KGreek project, strictly adhere to the established modular architecture. Follow these guidelines:

1. Module Responsibility Boundaries:
   - Configuration settings MUST be in config.py
   - Server implementation MUST be in server/
   - Request handlers MUST be in handlers/
   - Utility functions MUST be in utils/
   - XML processing MUST be in xml_utils/
   - Search functionality MUST be in search/
   - Import/export functionality MUST be in import_export/
   - Editor management MUST be in editor/

2. Separation of Concerns:
   - NEVER mix responsibilities across module boundaries
   - NEVER implement handler logic in server code
   - NEVER put configuration values in implementation modules
   - NEVER implement utility functions in domain-specific modules

3. Module Interface Guidelines:
   - ALWAYS update __init__.py files when adding new functionality
   - ALWAYS document public interfaces with proper docstrings
   - ALWAYS use relative imports for intra-package dependencies
   - ALWAYS make cross-module dependencies explicit through imports

4. Frontend/Backend Separation:
   - ALWAYS place CSS in static/css/
   - ALWAYS place JavaScript in static/js/
   - NEVER embed CSS or JavaScript directly in Python files

5. Backward Compatibility:
   - ALWAYS maintain compatibility with existing entry points
   - NEVER break existing API contracts
   - ALWAYS implement enhancements incrementally

6. XML Data Integrity:
   - ALWAYS treat XML files as the source of truth
   - NEVER modify XML processing without thorough testing

7. Code Organization:
   - Each file SHOULD have a single responsibility
   - Each function SHOULD do one thing well
   - Import order SHOULD be: standard library, third-party, local

These guidelines ensure maintainability, testability, and extensibility of the codebase while preserving the refactoring work that has been completed.
